course: dictionary
lesson: 9219
title: Words that name the doer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A solver is a person, or sometimes a program, that solves something. To solve means to find the answer. So a problem solver is someone who finds answers to problems. The ending -er often names the one who does the action, like a teacher teaches or a runner runs.
explain: «A good problem solver tries different ways, checks answers and does not give up.» The words around solver tell you what it does: tries, checks, does not give up. These clues help you work out the meaning before you look in a dictionary.
explain: Solver can also mean a program on a computer. «An online solver can work out an equation, but you still need to understand the steps.» The computer finds the answer, but you must still know how it got there. Test your meaning in the sentence: "an online program that finds the answer" still makes sense.
fact: A solver is a person who solves something, like a problem, puzzle or crime.
fact: In maths and computing, a solver is a program that finds answers to equations or puzzles.
fact: The ending -er often names the person or thing that does an action, as in «solver» from solve.
fact: «Keas», mountain parrots of New Zealand, are very curious puzzle solvers.
fact: Keas are known for pulling rubber off parked cars, because exploring everything pays off for them.
exercise: What does a solver do? | *Finds answers to problems or puzzles | Paints pictures of the sea | Sings songs in a choir
exercise: «A good problem solver tries different ways, checks answers and does not give up.» What do good solvers do? | They only ever guess | They try different ways and check their answers | *They try different ways and check their answers, and do not give up | They give up at the first try
exercise: An online solver can work out an equation. What must you still do? | Write the answer in a poem | Turn the computer off and forget the answer | *Understand the steps so you know how the answer was found
test: «Keas are very curious puzzle solvers.» What does puzzle solvers mean here? | Teachers who write puzzles | Cars that park by themselves | *Parrots that work out puzzles
test: Which is a solver in maths? | A teacher who gives homework | *A program that finds answers to equations | A word that means very old
exam: Which sentence uses solver correctly? | *Our class is full of good problem solvers who check their work | I am solver and I like football | A solver is a kind of cake | The solver is a loud brown bird that sings at night
